INSTRUCTION 0023 | 0x53 | c1 ff 1f | sar    edi,0x1f
  Section or entry point: dqrsl_.
  Long operation: Shift a 32-bit register right with sign fill and specify all defined and undefined flags.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Mask the immediate count 0x1f with 0x1f; effective count is 31. From the pre-instruction register bits, arithmetic-shift the original signed 32-bit value of edi right 31, replicating its original sign bit. Write the low 32-bit result to edi, clearing bits 63 through 32 of rdi. CF becomes original bit 30 (bit 0 is least significant), shifted out on the final step; SF is the result sign bit, ZF indicates zero result, PF is even parity of the low byte, AF is undefined and OF is undefined for this count greater than one. An effective count of zero would preserve the destination and all flags, but this instruction has nonzero effective count.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x56 (3 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

